<![CDATA[[XIC(Device[6].HMI_DeviceReset) ,XIC(HMI_AllReset) ][OTU(VF201.VFDCommsIntlk) ,OTU(VF201.VFDFaultIntlk) ,OTE(VF201_Small_Feeder_2:O.ClearFaults) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[FT103 High Pressure or Alarm Interlock — Always interlocks FT103. If FT103 is actively running in Auto, also interlocks the Auto process.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(FT103B.HighPressureInterlock) ,XIC(FT103B.Alarm) ]OTE(Device[7].Interlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[FT103 Interlock ID Reset — Sets Device[7] InterlockID to 0 when no FT103 device interlock is active.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Device[7].Interlock)MOV(0,Device[7].InterlockID);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[FT103 High Pressure Interlock ID — Sets Device[7] InterlockID to 50 when the High Pressure interlock is active. Inhibited during E-stop so E-stop ID 10 retains priority.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(EstopActive)XIC(FT103B.HighPressureInterlock)MOV(50,Device[7].InterlockID);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[FT103 Flowmeter Alarm Interlock ID — Sets Device[7] InterlockID to 40 when the flowmeter alarm is active. Inhibited during E-stop so E-stop ID 10 retains priority. ID 40 executes after ID 50 so the flowmeter alarm has priority over High Pressure.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(EstopActive)XIC(FT103B.Alarm)MOV(40,Device[7].InterlockID);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[FT103 Device Reset — Clears the latched High Pressure interlock when pressure is at or below the high-pressure limit and no flowmeter alarm is active. Final Device Interlock and InterlockID are derived from active causes.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Device[7].HMI_DeviceReset) ,XIC(HMI_AllReset) ]LEQ(PT103_PV_RAW,FT103B.HighPressureLimit_Int)XIO(FT103B.Alarm)OTU(FT103B.HighPressureInterlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[FT104 High Pressure or Alarm Interlock — Always interlocks FT104. If FT104 is actively running in Auto, also interlocks the Auto process.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(FT104B.HighPressureInterlock) ,XIC(FT104B.Alarm) ]OTE(Device[8].Interlock);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
